<title>DENMARK: Danish Nov current account deficit 6.6 bln DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish Nov current account deficit 6.6 bln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's current account swung into a 6.6 billion crown deficit in November against a revised 0.1 billion crown surplus in October, the national statistics office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH CURRENT ACCOUNT (billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Figures for the past three-, six- and 12-month periods:</p>
<p>(Billions of crowns)</p>
<p>		     Three-month Six-month Twelve-month</p>
<p>Current account   -3.4	  +0.2	  +8.4</p>
<p>Goods		+10.1	 +20.3	 +38.8</p>
<p>Services	    -0.8	  +1.9	  +6.2</p>
<p>Interest, other  -12.7	 -22.0	 -36.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are subject to rounding. Market analysts polled by Reuters had predicted an average November current account deficit of 5.2 billion crowns. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969650</p>
</text>
